sentences.text:
So far non- pecuniary damages are concerned, they may include (i) damages for MACT No.:1051/19 Roshan v. Rajesh kumar Gupta & Or Page No. 9 of 24 mental and physical shock, pain and suffering, already suffered or likely to be suffered in future;
(ii) damages to compensate for the loss of amenities of life which may include a variety of matters i.e. on account of injury the claimant may not be able to walk, run or sit; (iii) damages for the loss of expectation of life, i.e., on account of injury the normal longevity of the person concerned is shortened; (iv) inconvenience, hardship,
discomfort, disappointment, frustration and mental stress in life."
